.TH CHIMP-LOOP 1 "2026-11" "chimp 0.7.0"
.SH NAME
chimp-loop \- play a drum kit from a MIDI controller and loop it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chimp-loop
.br
.B chimp-loop
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chimp-loop
is a drum machine for any MIDI controller: 16 parts, live looping and step entry on one
pattern, a sound per pad and a master bus.
.PP
Press Record, play, press Record again to close the loop (or pick a length in bars and it
closes on its own); press Record again to overdub a layer, Undo to remove the last one.
The step grid (16 steps a bar) toggles hits and cycles their velocity. Quantise (1/4 to
1/32) and swing are applied on playback, so they can change after recording.
.PP
Each pad has level, pan, pitch, attack, sustain, decay, a resonant low/high/band-pass
filter, drive (soft, hard, fuzz, crush), punch, reverse, and sends to the master delay
and reverb. The master has a tempo-synced ping-pong delay, a reverb (hall, octave-up
or octave-down shimmer, reverse), drive, a resonant DJ filter, a compressor and a
brick-wall limiter, with presets.
.PP
Notes 36\(en51 play sounds 1\(en16 (an LPD8 program on notes 36\(en43 plays the first
eight); any pad or button can be assigned to a sound or to a looper control. Loops can
be saved, and exported as WAV or as a standard MIDI file (General MIDI drum notes on
channel 10).
.SH KNOBS
CC 70\(en77 (the LPD8 mk2's knobs out of the box) are eight knobs on a page: the selected
pad (level, pitch, attack, decay, cutoff, resonance, drive, reverb send) or the master
(filter, resonance, drive, delay, echoes, reverb, size, compress). K switches page. Any
parameter can be given its own knob or fader in the window. While the LPD8 is on a
program with desktop actions (see
.BR chimpd (1)),
the looper ignores it.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Space
Record, close the loop, overdub on/off.
.TP
.B Enter
Play / stop.
.TP
.B Backspace
Undo the last layer.
.TP
.BR Delete " or " Ctrl+Backspace
Clear the loop.
.TP
.B T
Tap tempo.
.TP
.B K
Switch the knob page (pad / master).
.TP
.B [ ]
Previous / next saved sound.
.TP
.B G
Hold for roll: held pads repeat on the beat.
.TP
.B 5 6 7 8
Hold: stutter 1/4, 1/8, 1/16, 1/32.
.TP
.B 9 0 \-
Hold: tape stop, reverse, half speed.
.TP
.BR Shift ", " Ctrl ", " Alt " + a pad key"
Select, mute, solo that part.
.TP
.B Z X C V, A S D F, Q W E R, 1 2 3 4
Sounds 1\(en16, laid out like the pads.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/chimp/loop.json
Settings and assignments.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/chimp/loops/
Saved loops.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/chimp/kits/<name>/
Your own kits (the built-in one, synth, is synthesised): a folder of WAVs and a
.I kit.yaml
naming the WAV, label and General MIDI note for each pad. Without kit.yaml, files
named kick, snare_1, clap, hihat_1, open_hihat, rim, tom_1, crash, snare_2,
hihat_2, tom_2, tom_3, ride, perc_1, perc_2, perc_3 go to those pads and others
fill the gaps. Kits are imported (a folder, a .chimpkit or a .zip), made empty
and filled pad by pad, and exported as .chimpkit files (a zipped kit folder) from
the app. Replaced samples are moved to the kit's
.I replaced/
folder.
.TP
.I ~/Music/Chimp/
Exports.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PIPEWIRE_LATENCY
Defaults to 256/48000 for this program, for about 11 ms from pad to sound.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chimp (1),
.BR chimpd (1)
